[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105612,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Desmoid fibromatosis is a locally aggressive, non-metastasizing (myo)fibroblastic neoplasm with a high propensity for local recurrence.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105613,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8821/1 Extra-abdominal desmoid</p>\r\n<p>8822/1 Abdominal fibromatosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105614,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F7C &amp; XH13Z3 Neoplasms of uncertain behaviour of connective or other soft tissue &amp; Desmoid-type fibromatosis (aggressive fibromatosis)</p>\r\n<p>2F7C &amp; XH6116 Neoplasms of uncertain behaviour of connective or other soft tissue &amp; Abdominal (mesenteric) fibromatosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105615,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> aggressive fibromatosis; desmoid tumour.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> musculoaponeurotic fibromatosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105616,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Extra-abdominal desmoid; abdominal fibromatosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105617,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In childhood, desmoid fibromatosis predominantly occurs in the extremities, head/neck, and trunk {1946077; 19950127; 24206198}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105618,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with desmoid fibromatosis present with a slow-growing deep-seated mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105619,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Desmoid fibromatosis is rare, affecting &lt;&nbsp;4&nbsp;patients per 1&nbsp;million person-years and accounting for approximately 2&ndash;3% of soft tissue tumours in children {7091046; 1946077; 19950127; 22924016; 28209418}. The peak incidence in childhood is between the ages of 6&nbsp;and 15&nbsp;years {19950127}. There is no sex predominance in paediatric patients.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105620,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Genetic, physical, and hormonal factors are involved in the etiology of desmoid tumours {28961825}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105621,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The majority (90&ndash;95%) of sporadic desmoid tumours result from mutations in <em>CTNNB1</em>, the gene that encodes &beta;-catenin {17721184; 18832571; 23913621; 20197769; 26171757}. Less commonly, desmoid tumours arise in the setting of familial adenomatous polyposis (germline mutations in the <em>APC</em> tumour suppressor gene) {10094547; 11241320; 8150351; 18722078; 15095846}. Aberrations in <em>CTNNB1</em> or <em>APC</em> lead to nuclear &beta;-catenin accumulation, resulting in increased activation of the WNT/&beta;-catenin pathway and tumorigenesis {19436199; 28575679; 17952864}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105622,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Desmoid fibromatosis is firm and poorly circumscribed, with a grey/tan whorled cut surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105623,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histological examination reveals bland (myo)fibroblasts arranged in long, sweeping fascicles with an infiltrative growth pattern. Approximately 20% have an associated Gardner fibroma {17325483; 25064609}. The lesional cells typically show tram-track staining for SMA, and the majority (80%) show nuclear &beta;-catenin expression.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105624,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cytological findings are nonspecific {8498134}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105625,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>&beta;-catenin mutation analysis may be helpful in small biopsies and/or when &beta;-catenin immunostaining is difficult to interpret {21884214; 22766794}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105626,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> infiltrative long, sweeping fascicles of bland fibroblasts and myofibroblasts.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> nuclear &beta;-catenin expression; <em>CTNNB1</em> mutation (in challenging cases or small biopsies).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105627,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105628,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 492,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The behaviour of desmoid fibromatosis is variable with unpredictable growth, stabilization, and regression {19950127}. Local recurrence does not consistently correlate with surgical margin status, and a watchful waiting approach is suggested for asymptomatic patients {21844500; 22419028; 28961825}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]